    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) across the app:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipTier` string property from the `Owner` schema and added `membershipLevel` as a read-only `int32` (min 1, max 3). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getMembershipLevel()/setMembershipLevel()`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier(Owner)` method and its `@Mapping` with `membershipLevel(Owner)`, implementing the new algorithm: start at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. (Level 4 is left reserved for tenure, as noted.)\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel` (computed via the mapper) instead of the old tier. The confirming log line shows `membershipLevel=3`. I also dropped the now-obsolete comment on `countHouseholdMembers` that referenced the removed `GOLD` tier \u2014 the level no longer depends on household size.\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipLevel` of 3 for an owner with an email and no namesakes) passes.\n\nNote: `Owner.householdMemberCount` is now set but no longer read by any logic (it previously only fed the GOLD tier). I left the field and its plumbing in place since removing it is outside the scope of this change and harmless, but it's effectively dead now \u2014 worth cleaning up separately if you'd like.",
